{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1461667-tying-my-player\u2019s-deaths-together","id":1461667,"title":"Tying my player\u2019s deaths together","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-27T05:22:14-07:00","id":1461667,"title":"Tying my player\u2019s deaths together","content":"Just started running a new game with four players and have completed psyche creation, we did a little shadow but left it incomplete until next week.<br /> <br /> The setting is a fictional English costal city in modern day. 6GM has not happened.<br /> <br /> We have a 15 year old homeless immigrant from an Asian country (unspecified) who worked essentially as a slave on a fishing ship. They got sick during a long voyage and their work suffered, and as a concequence was killed by the captain during the night and thrown overboard.<br /> They regret that they did not know their family and also wishes to get revenge on the captain. Their fetters include their best friend a fellow child slave (13 years old), the port, and a letter to their family as well as a mystery fetter.<br /> Only one to invest in castigate and life web, so the circle is going to rely on them a lot. Also has puppetry. As a 2 point haunt which they haven\u2019t yet specified what it is. Possibly the harbour?<br /> <br /> A sweet poet who actually revels in manipulating people into doing what she wants. Very involved in community projects and regularly gave lectures at a university one town over, where works their live interest, whom they never had the chance to confess their feelings to. They died mysteriously and have a passion to uncover truths, protected their loved ones, and preserve their reputation.<br /> Love interest is a fetter, as is a lighthouse which they sometimes wondered by for inspiration, which they took also as their haunt. another fetter is their study at home and a notebook of their unfinished works. Being a manipulator type character, they took Intimation, mnemosynis, and puppetry, and has all the makings of a really terrifying character.<br /> <br /> A woman who has been sold off to a rich family where they essentially lived as an ornament. They are 5 point appearance and their adopted family never let her develop her own personality. She used Belladonna to enhance her eyes to better fit with her role as a beautiful thing for her adoptive family to show off. I\u2019ll never to dig a bit deeper but at one point their character in a fit of rage broke a priceless piece of artwork and has felt guilty about it ever since, their use of belladonna became excessive until they died of an overdose.<br /> Her main regrets are having hurt her adoptive family and her passions are to protect them, bring joy to her bio father, and to compensate the victims of her outburst (again I need to get more details on this.)<br /> Biodad is a fetter, as is the family home and the library computer, they also opted for a mystery fetter. They too nicked up intimation and mnenosynis, but also opted for embody.<br /> <br /> Lastly is an artist who left hole 15 years ago to try to make it in the art world. Their father died 10 years ago, but never went home, being too busy trying to get their big break. They died shortly after getting their painting into a gallery for the first time mysteriously and regret both that they never got to achieve success, and that they didn\u2019t spend more time with their mother. He wishes to be remembered, discover what happened to him, find somewhere to call home. And make amends with their family. Fetters include their mother, their family home, and the painting which currently hangs in the gallery and serves as part of a 3 point legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, I already have a few ideas on how to connect them. The family that owns the woman may own a fishing fleet and thus benefit by the exploiting of the young fishing slave. While it\u2019s not unlikely that the painter and the poet may have crossed paths in academic circles.<br /> <br /> Bridging the two together is going to be a bit more tricky. Perhaps the rich family that owns the fishing fleet also haze a stake in the gallery? Perhaps the love interest of the poet is related to a member of the family?<br /> <br /> Also, it\u2019s interesting that two have mysterious deaths, while the other two have mystery fetters. It gives me a lot of room to forge ties between them as they discover the key to these mysteries.<br /> <br /> One concept I had before character creation was they would all be reaped by a Victorian era free wraith who unbeknownst to them was responsible for the circumstances of each if their deaths through a mixture of catharsis and repeat violations of the dictum mortum. They would reap them out of guilt as a way to atone for having caused their deaths, but is too ashamed to tell them. The idea is, as these are mostly new players, the free wraith would act as a seemingly benevolent figure who would slowly introduce some concepts to the players and wraiths alike.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking of giving them Usury and Argos to complement what\u2019s missing in the circle, as well as outrage and possibly puppetry to give them ways to interfere with the skinlands.<br /> <br /> Their story initially was that their wife died in childbirth and they held resentment towards their son as a result. They were bitter and cruel to them all through their life until, close to death, we began to feel a great remorse. He tried to leave everything he had to his son, but upon dying, his son, a now fully grown man, refused it all. What\u2019s worse is his wife had long fell to oblvion and has become a spectre who tries to push guilt onto the Victorian free wraith.<br /> <br /> I would like some ideas on how I can ties all their deaths to the Victorian wraith. Any ideas or thoughts would be appreciated, especially concerning how the mystery deaths happened.<br /> <br /> As I type this, one idea that jumps to mind is the Victorian wraiths family is this rich family, and that he skinrode people in order to ensure that his family would eventually receive the inheritance and so had a direct hand in forging this group.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m still unsure how this might relate to the mystery deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-27-2021, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T08:31:34-07:00","id":1462799,"title":"","content":"Outsource it. Someone else is predominantly responsible for the mystery deaths, but Mr. Benefactor is involved somehow. For instance, perhaps his family gave rise to some kind of abuser who targets and sometimes kills artists. The benefactor is aiding and/or protecting him and possibly subtly pointing him in certain directions.<br /> <br /> One twist I might pull is that when they figure out that he is linked to their killer, he doesn't even deny it. Instead he claims to be mentoring them to make up for what his family member did and the only reason he didn't tell them is to avoid giving their shadows Angst. This would be, at best, a partial truth, but believable enough.<br /> <br /> The advantage of outsourcing it is that you don't have to figure out how four deaths fit in perfectly with his master plan. It gives him a point of weakness where events are outside his control, but it also means his entire story doesn't fall apart at the first revelation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T13:57:27-07:00","id":1462836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1461667-tying-my-player\u2019s-deaths-together?p=1462799#post1462799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outsource it. Someone else is predominantly responsible for the mystery deaths, but Mr. Benefactor is involved somehow. For instance, perhaps his family gave rise to some kind of abuser who targets and sometimes kills artists. The benefactor is aiding and/or protecting him and possibly subtly pointing him in certain directions.<br /> <br /> One twist I might pull is that when they figure out that he is linked to their killer, he doesn't even deny it. Instead he claims to be mentoring them to make up for what his family member did and the only reason he didn't tell them is to avoid giving their shadows Angst. This would be, at best, a partial truth, but believable enough.<br /> <br /> The advantage of outsourcing it is that you don't have to figure out how four deaths fit in perfectly with his master plan. It gives him a point of weakness where events are outside his control, but it also means his entire story doesn't fall apart at the first revelation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the week since I\u2019ve posted this, I\u2019ve come up with a few ideas on how to connect everyone.<br /> <br /> The free wraith\u2019s family is abusive and neglectful of the girl, this neglect is something which we gave to his son, and has since passed it down the line.<br /> They also began the shipping industry that rose on cheap labour, which morphed towards slavery as labour laws changed over time. The family run it at an arms length, and the wraith protects them from any legal trouble via puppetry.<br /> The other two deaths were more direct. As a concequence of his son\u2019s hatred of him, he changed his name and with it a large amount of the wraith\u2019s legacy fell away with them. The one legacy that is still theirs is their name on the wing of a gallery, which is struggling. The same gallery the artist managed to give their art to.<br /> During a fit of catharsis, the wraith jumped into an unsuspecting person and proceeded to stalk the artist and then beat him half to death, with the shadow only relenting to let the wraith take the final blow, knowing that their death would likely catapult the net value of the art, saving the gallery and thus protecting their legacy.<br /> <br /> All the while, their wife is taunting them with how much pain the wraith is causing. He chases after her with intent to destroy her, and she calls a few of her spectre associates to give him something to fight. He loses himself in a fit of rage as she leads towards a seemingly empty pier. He sees her standing there with that same side taunting smile, and he prepares to obliviate her. And she disappears just at the last moment, revealing the artist just behind her. But it\u2019s too late to pull back, and his attack pierces the shroud, hitting her full force (5 agg), causing her to fly backwards into the sea (2 bash). She doesn\u2019t die immediately, instead she floats there semiconscious and the wraith stares at her and watches as her aura weakens, guilt and regret etched across his face. All will to fight completely lost.<br /> <br /> His wife laughs at his remorse, reminding him of how little he cared in life when he caused suffering, and how odd it was that he cared so much about this one whom he had never known prior, and once they cross the shroud she muses on how easily they\u2019ll fall to oblivion, same as him.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when he pledges to make amends, to help those his acts have cursed to roam the shadowlands, stalked by the very spectre that taunts him now. She finds that very amusing, considering what a terrible father he was in life, and so agrees, and gathers up their cauls for him to find and reap, intentionally placing them outside the city so he has to hunt them before the hierarchy finds them, or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}